# Copy this template to BASE_PATH/configs/albis.env (ignored by Git); never commit populated files.
# Replace 100 (tenant) and 120 (shop) with the actual SiteContext IDs.
# Each tenant/shop/environment requires a separate, complete set of all three values.
# A valid file set takes priority; otherwise a complete, valid getenv() set is used.
# Values from different sources, shops, tenants or environments are never combined.
# Missing, unreadable or malformed files and incomplete/invalid sets fall back as a whole.
# Without a valid set from either source, leasing calculation stays disabled.
# PHP-FPM only needs environment forwarding when using the getenv() alternative.
#
# Format: INI-compatible KEY=VALUE, preferably double-quoted values as below.
# Values are literal (no shell/variable/constant expansion); empty values are not credentials.
# Use one assignment per line and # or ; for full-line comments. No export, sections,
# arrays, duplicate keys or multiline values. Do not execute/source this file as PHP or shell code.
DEWAWI_ALBIS_100_120_TEST_CLIENT_ID=""
DEWAWI_ALBIS_100_120_TEST_CLIENT_SECRET=""
DEWAWI_ALBIS_100_120_TEST_CACHE_KEY=""
DEWAWI_ALBIS_100_120_LIVE_CLIENT_ID=""
DEWAWI_ALBIS_100_120_LIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=""
DEWAWI_ALBIS_100_120_LIVE_CACHE_KEY=""
# CACHE_KEY: base64 of 32 cryptographically random bytes, generated separately per scope:
# php -r 'echo base64_encode(random_bytes(32)), PHP_EOL;'
# Copy only the generated value between the quotes; it is not an ALBIS API credential.
#
# Permissions: configs directory 0750, albis.env 0600 owned by the PHP worker user,
# or 0640 owned by a trusted administrator with a dedicated PHP-readable group.
# Grant the PHP worker read access; never make the file or directory world-readable/writable.
# The repository .htaccess blocks all /configs HTTP access, including existing files.
# Apache must honor this .htaccess (AllowOverride for its directives and mod_rewrite enabled).
# On Nginx enforce the equivalent in the actual server configuration, for example:
# location ^~ /configs/ { deny all; }
# Adapt the prefix for subdirectory installations; check that GET/HEAD/POST return 403/404.
# PHP's development server does not enforce .htaccess: never expose the repository with it.
# Never expose credentials through phpinfo, HTTP responses, logs, backups or SQL dumps.
# No runtime web-server configuration or populated credential file is installed by this template.
#
# Tokens are AES-256-GCM encrypted in Zend_Cache; refresh tokens are discarded.
# Cache TTL: access token <= 600s (30s expiry margin), master data 3600s, quotes 900s,
# unavailable conditions 300s, API/network failures 60s. Credential/key rotation changes cache scope.
# Apply the ALBIS additions in update-1.1.7-1.1.8.sql before enabling.
# If that upgrade has already run, apply only its two new ALBIS ALTER statements after schema inspection.
# Admin > Shop > ALBIS Leasing: default disabled, threshold > EUR 5000 net, group 23, contract 1, payment 2.
# Confirm the actual one-time net processing fee with ALBIS, explicitly entering 0 when agreed.
# Require catalog/inquiry entitlements and explicitly mark each financeable article as eligible.
# Confirm group 23 (commercial kitchen equipment) matches the products and is enabled for the live account.
# Seller-specific master data checks gate calculation. Final live credential/condition acceptance is manual.
# Production suppresses test quotes. Test using APPLICATION_ENV=development with the test environment.
# Public specs (identical on 2026-11-19):
# https://test-api.albis-leasing.de/openapi.json
# https://api.albis-leasing.de/openapi.json
# SHA256 for both: e7ba4aa27a4d9c6f85276c33913fad059e05ab619965d4c71d8282b0bb2e80ea
# Response description uses {raten: [...]}; response example is [...]. Both are accepted.
# No application endpoint, customer data transmission or checkout integration is implemented.
